==French==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|fr|chaine||post-1990}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|fr|frm|chaisne}}, from {{inh|fr|fro|chaene}}, {{m|fro|chaiene}}, {{m|fro|caiene}}, inherited from {{inh|fr|la|catēna}}. {{doublet|fr|cadène|catène}}. The long vowel derives from the Old French hiatus; by analogy the length expressed with a silent ''-s-'' in Middle French, which was then replaced with the circumflex.

